# Revisions to skip when running `git blame`.
#
# Only bulk, mechanical, no-behaviour-change commits belong here — a
# repo-wide reformat, a mass rename, a license-header sweep. Never add a
# commit that changes what the code does.
#
# GitHub reads this file automatically for its web blame view. Local `git
# blame` does not, so enable it once per clone:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# (Relative paths in that setting resolve from the repository root, so the
# same one-liner works from any subdirectory.)
#
# This repo squash-merges, so a SHA added on a feature branch is not the SHA
# that lands on `main`. Re-point each entry at the squashed commit once the
# PR that introduced it is merged. An entry naming a commit `main` does not
# have is inert, not fatal — git only rejects lines that are not valid object
# names — so a stale entry degrades blame quietly rather than breaking it.

